WEBVTT

s1-phone-scorecard
00:00:01.200 --> 00:00:20.430
Casey, the assigned scorekeeper, opens the FLI demonstration event on a phone. The scorecard already knows the setup: Round 1 · 9 holes · Red, an intermission, then Round 2 · 9 holes · Blue — with Group 1's two teams and their four athletes.

s2-draft-and-submit
00:00:22.830 --> 00:00:42.470
On hole 1 of Round 1, Casey enters strokes — every entry saves as a draft. One score is still blank, and the card says exactly why that matters: missing scores block submission and never count as zero. Casey fills it in, and Round 1 is submitted.

s3-second-pass
00:00:44.870 --> 00:01:02.790
After the intermission, Round 2 replays the same nine physical holes at the Blue positions. The card displays holes 10 through 18 — displayed hole 10 is physical hole 1 on the second pass — and each round's scores stay separate.

s4-final-hole
00:01:05.190 --> 00:01:21.310
Later in the round, the card is nearly complete. Casey enters the final scores on hole 18 and submits Round 2. Submitted scorecards are locked against silent changes — official approval and published results arrive in Phase 1H.
